# Build and Testing Procedures

## Build Commands
- Use `make all` to build for current platform and Linux x86_64
- Use `go build -o main` for local development builds
- Cross-compile with `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build`

## Testing
- Run tests with `make test`
- Tests are filtered to exclude generated files and external packages
- Use `go test -v -run '(Test|Example)'` pattern
- Test all packages except `/tests`, `/xcpb`, `/gpb`, `/generated`

## Code Quality
- Use `go fmt` for code formatting
- Run `go vet` for static analysis
- Use `golint` for linting (if available)
- Check for unused imports and variables

## Dependencies
- Keep dependencies up to date with `go mod tidy`
- Use specific versions for critical dependencies
- Document any version constraints in [go.mod](mdc:go.mod)
- Test with different Go versions for compatibility

## Cleanup
- Use `make clean` to remove build artifacts
- Remove `main` and `main_x86_64` binaries
- Clean up any temporary files or logs
